# HISTORICAL FORK (1980 vs 1983). In Release 88 the parser infers
# the instrument and "light candles" just works. Release 2's parser
# demands it spelled out: a bare "light candles" asks "You must tell
# me what to light them with" -- and the match burns out during the
# question, so the ceremony silently fails and the spirits stay.
#
# Bonus discovery from probing this fork: Release 2 has a latent bug
# of its own. Typing "light candles" while the candles are still on
# the ground (the red-hot bell makes you drop them) runs a code path
# that pops a stack value it never pushed. Infocom's 1980 flat-stack
# interpreters silently read a caller's value and carried on; a
# Standard-strict interpreter halts, per section 15's rule for pull.
# Reproduce from this point with:
#   x candles / x bell / ring bell / light match / light candles
# So: take the candles first, and name the match.

light candles with match
read book

s
get skull
